in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @smarts
in @reflection
in @frame
in @moi
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic

# @smarts/reflection — the substrate-architectural ${\leftrightarrow}$
# observability adapter species.
#
# Tick 36 of the refined /loop discipline. Tick 35's residue (Seam C1
# from the @reflection family-root review): the family-root header
# claimed "composes-with @smarts at substrate-architectural altitude"
# without a mechanical realization. This species IS that realization
# — the typed adapter that bridges @smarts's substrate-architectural
# integration form (`smarts` record per shards/smarts.mirror) to
# @reflection's per-tick observability surface (`observation` record
# per shards/reflection.mirror).
#
# CRQ: how does @reflection's observability surface admit a @smarts
# instance as an observable WITHOUT violating either family's discipline?
#
# Answer: the adapter species declares a typed bridge carrier and
# typed bridge action. @smarts.ratify produces a discipline-flexible
# smarts instance; @reflection.observe takes a frame + residue. The
# bridge converts the smarts instance into an observation by mapping
# the smarts's substrate-architectural integration as the @reflection
# frame; the residue is the unratified portion of the smarts instance
# (the substrate-decl candidates the @reflection loop's next tick
# will process).
#
# === The adapter pattern (Seam-verified per @magic family) ===
#
# @magic/distinction (tick 15) + @magic/frame (tick 27) established
# the cross-family adapter pattern for the @magic family:
# - typed bridge carrier (record over both families' typed forms)
# - typed bridge action (consumes one family, produces the other's
#   typed input)
# - bilateral predicate that ratifies the bridge's coherence under
#   perturbation
# - composes-with framing (NOT structural identity)
#
# This adapter applies the same pattern at @smarts ↔ @reflection.
# Sixth instance of the cross-family adapter discipline (after
# distinction → magic; frame → magic; @smarts/reflection sibling
# adapters forward-promised at shards/smarts/{magic,frame,cyberpunk,
# kintsugi}.mirror).
#
# === Closes Seam C1 from tick 35 ===
#
# Seam's tick-35 C1 finding (paraphrased): "@reflection family-root
# claimed `composes-with` @smarts but provides no mechanical adapter;
# the substrate-architectural integration claim is aspirational."
# This species closes that finding by:
#
# 1. Declaring the typed bridge carrier (smarts_reflection_bridge).
# 2. Declaring the typed bridge action that converts @smarts.smarts
#    into @reflection.observation.
# 3. Naming the bilateral predicate `bridge_coherent` first-consumed
#    by the bridge action via `requires`.
# 4. Composing-with @smarts.discipline_flexible at the bridge
#    boundary: bridging is only admissible from a discipline-flexible
#    smarts.
#
# Per Seam B1 closure pattern: the bridge action IS the FIRST non-
# decorative consumer of `bridge_coherent`; the predicate is not
# paint.
#
# === Substrate-pull-correct home ===
#
# Per the species naming convention: cross-family adapters land at
# `shards/<family-A>/<family-B>.mirror` (the family-A subspecies of
# family-B). This shard at `shards/smarts/reflection.mirror` declares
# `@smarts/reflection` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.
#
# Forward-promised siblings (per smarts.mirror header):
# - shards/smarts/magic.mirror       — @smarts ↔ @magic adapter
# - shards/smarts/frame.mirror       — @smarts ↔ @frame adapter
# - shards/smarts/cyberpunk.mirror   — @smarts ↔ @cyberpunk adapter
# - shards/smarts/epistemologic.mirror — @smarts ↔ @epistemologic/
#                                       cybernetic adapter
# - shards/smarts/kintsugi.mirror    — @smarts ↔ @kintsugi adapter
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   adapter pattern              Gang of Four design patterns (1994).
#                                The cross-system bridge pattern at
#                                programming altitude.
#   bridge pattern               Gang of Four design patterns (1994).
#                                Decoupling abstraction from
#                                implementation; the substrate-
#                                architectural analogue.
#   natural transformation       Category theory; Eilenberg-MacLane
#                                1945. The mathematical structure of
#                                a structure-preserving map between
#                                functors; this adapter IS the natural
#                                transformation between @smarts's and
#                                @reflection's substrate-architectural
#                                forms.
#   functor composition          The @smarts ↔ @reflection adapter IS
#                                a functor between the two families'
#                                substrate-decl categories.
#
# Spec context: shards/reflection.mirror (the @reflection family-root
#               whose composes-with claim this adapter realizes);
#               shards/smarts.mirror (the @smarts family-root whose
#               header forward-promised this species);
#               docs/specs/reflection-model.md (the spec @reflection
#               lifts).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-reflection-as-compiler]] (#85;
#                       this adapter closes the substrate-architectural
#                       integration claim);
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; the bridge IS the
#                       boundary-harness at the cross-family @io),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull-confidence-acts]]
#                       (the discipline today's cascade runs).
# Related shards: smarts.mirror (the @smarts family-root; declares
#                  smarts + ratify + discipline_flexible the bridge
#                  consumes),
#                 reflection.mirror (the @reflection family-root;
#                  declares observation + observe the bridge
#                  produces),
#                 magic/distinction.mirror (Spencer-Brown adapter
#                  precedent; tick 15),
#                 magic/frame.mirror (@magic ↔ @frame adapter
#                  precedent; tick 27).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/smarts/reflection.mirror`
# declares `@smarts/reflection` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/gamma-helm-johnson-vlissides-1994
source @arxiv/category-theory/eilenberg-maclane-1945

glass @smarts/reflection {
  focus reflection
  project reflection
  split reflection
  shift reflection
  settle reflection
}

# === The smarts_reflection_bridge carrier ===
#
# Per Seam tick-30 C4 closure pattern: typed record over both
# families' carriers, not bare ref. The substrate-architectural
# bridge IS the record carrying:
#
# - smarts_form  : the @smarts instance being bridged (substrate-
#                  architectural integration form)
# - frame_form   : the @frame the @reflection loop operates in (per
#                  recognition #82; per-tick cognitive-order state)
# - observation  : the @reflection observation produced by the bridge
# - pact_witness : the @moi composition-time pact-witness ratifying
#                  the bridge respects both families' disciplines
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the quadruple.
type smarts_reflection_bridge = {
  smarts_form:  smarts,
  frame_form:   frame,
  observation:  observation,
  pact_witness: ref,
}

# === bridge action (FIRST non-decorative consumer of bridge_coherent) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at @smarts/reflection altitude. Converts a
# @smarts instance (substrate-architectural integration form) plus a
# @frame (the @reflection loop's per-tick state) into a @reflection
# observation (the substrate-architectural integration's observable
# trace).
#
# Takes s (the @smarts), f (the @frame), p (the perturbation under
# which the bridge is checked); returns the typed observation that
# @reflection.observe-style downstream processing consumes.
#
# requires bridge_coherent(...): the bridge maintains both families'
# disciplines under perturbation. Composes
# @smarts.discipline_flexible + @frame.bounded_commutator_check +
# @reflection's bilateral structure at the cross-family boundary per
# alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual bridging
# is implemented by composing @smarts.ratify + @frame's per-tick
# state extraction + @reflection.observe's observation construction.
bridge(s: smarts, f: frame, p: perturbation) -> observation
requires bridge_coherent(s, f, p)
{ \ }

# === bridge_coherent predicate (bilateral) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) AND the
# cross-family adapter discipline.
#
# Per Seam B1 closure pattern: bridge action (above) is the FIRST non-
# decorative consumer via `requires bridge_coherent(s, f, p)`.
#
# Consumer shards (forward-promised at @smarts/reflection species + the
# other sibling adapters) name `requires bridge_coherent(s, f, p)` to
# declare bilateral agreement that the cross-family bridge maintains
# both families' disciplines under perturbation.
#
# Discharge: substrate-pull-correct cross-family coherence check at
# the species boundary. Bounded → both families' disciplines are
# preserved across the bridge (admit composition); unbounded → the
# bridge violates one or both families' disciplines (bridging refused).
#
# Same shape as the bilateral predicates the prior families carry:
# - @magic: invariant_preserved, audited, mechanism_intact
# - @frame: bounded_commutator_check
# - @smarts: discipline_flexible
# - @cyberpunk: cybernetic_coherence
# - @pack: pack_coherent
# - @pack/seam: review_sound
# - @moi: pact_respected
# - @reflection: loss_decreases, speaks_at_n_plus_1
# - @smarts/reflection: bridge_coherent (this one)
bridge_coherent(s: smarts, f: frame, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

out @smarts/reflection
out smarts_reflection_bridge
out bridge
out bridge_coherent
